Q: How to detect Impeller or Skia in Flutter app? A: <p>Here is how to check whether an app is running with Impeller or Skia:</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>// 🎯 Dart imports:
import 'dart:ui' as ui;

class RenderingUtils {
    static bool isShaderFilterSupported() {
        // True only when the Impeller engine is active.
        return ui.ImageFilter.isShaderFilterSupported;
    }

    static String rendererName() =&gt; isShaderFilterSupported() ? 'Impeller' : 'Skia';
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>2026 update:</strong></p>
<p>Flutter appears to be logging renderer engine used during app launch:</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>[IMPORTANT:flutter/shell/platform/embedder/embedder_surface_metal_impeller.mm(51)] Using the Impeller rendering backend (Metal).
</code></pre>

Q: Set OpenID Connect CallbackPath to HTTPS A: <p><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/users/1839439/dharman">Dharman</a>'s answer with a custom <code>OnRedirectToIdentityProvider</code> is one part of the puzzle, but it will not work for sign out. When you sign out the Auth0's sign out event builds a url based on the request (using the http scheme) and appends it to a redirect as a <code>returnTo</code> query param. I did not see a way to influence this behavior.</p>
<p>The solution I found is to create a custom sign out event. Since this runs after the Auth0 event, you can directly modify the full redirect url like this. I will share my full solution which handles both sign in and sign out.</p>
<pre><code>    /// &lt;summary&gt;
    ///     Change redirect_url from http to https when behind load balancer with ssl termination
    /// &lt;/summary&gt;
    public static readonly Func&lt;RedirectContext, Task&gt; CustomOnRedirectToIdentityProviderEvent = (context) =&gt;
        {
            var env = context.HttpContext.RequestServices.GetRequiredService&lt;IWebHostEnvironment&gt;();
            if (!env.IsDevelopment())
            {
                var request = context.Request;
                var httpsUri = context.ProtocolMessage.RedirectUri ?? &quot;/&quot;;
                if (httpsUri.StartsWith('/'))
                {
                    httpsUri = $&quot;{request.Scheme}://{request.Host}{request.PathBase}{httpsUri}&quot;;
                }
                httpsUri = httpsUri.Replace(&quot;http://&quot;, &quot;https://&quot;);

                context.ProtocolMessage.RedirectUri = httpsUri;
            }

            return Task.CompletedTask;
        };

    /// &lt;summary&gt;
    ///     Change ?returnTo= query param in redirect from http to https when behind load balancer with ssl termination
    /// &lt;/summary&gt;
    public static readonly Func&lt;RedirectContext, Task&gt; CustomOnRedirectToIdentityProviderForSignOutEvent = (context) =&gt;
        {
            var env = context.HttpContext.RequestServices.GetRequiredService&lt;IWebHostEnvironment&gt;();
            if (!env.IsDevelopment())
            {
                var redirectUrl = context.Response.Headers[&quot;Location&quot;].ToString();
                redirectUrl = redirectUrl.Replace(Uri.EscapeDataString(&quot;http://&quot;), Uri.EscapeDataString(&quot;https://&quot;));

                context.Response.Headers[&quot;Location&quot;] = redirectUrl;
            }

            return Task.CompletedTask;
        };
</code></pre>
<p>Add them both to the Auth0 setup in startup:</p>
<pre><code>builder.Services.AddAuth0WebAppAuthentication(options =&gt;
{
    ...
    options.OpenIdConnectEvents = new OpenIdConnectEvents
    {
        OnRedirectToIdentityProvider = CustomAuthFunctions.CustomOnRedirectToIdentityProviderEvent,
        OnRedirectToIdentityProviderForSignOut = CustomAuthFunctions.CustomOnRedirectToIdentityProviderForSignOutEvent,
    };
});
</code></pre>
